Other credited work
===================

database-access uses PubMed (NCBI E-utilities) (https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils), a service by National Center for Biotechnology Information; terms: NLM public-domain utility service; terms: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK25501/ (as BioMCP 0.9.3's source inventory records it, reviewed 2026-04-10).

database-access uses Crossref REST API (https://api.crossref.org), a service by Crossref; terms: No sign-up is needed, almost none of the metadata is subject to copyright and it may be used for any purpose, though some abstracts may be under their publishers' or authors' copyright; the polite pool asks for a mailto address (Crossref REST API page, https://www.crossref.org/documentation/retrieve-metadata/rest-api/, read 2026-11-27).

database-access uses OpenAlex API (https://api.openalex.org), a service by OurResearch; terms: OpenAlex data is under CC0, in the public domain (attribution appreciated, not required); free API use is capped at 100,000 credits a day and 100 requests a second, more on a paid plan (OpenAlex's documentation source, ourresearch/openalex-docs license.md and how-to-use-the-api/rate-limits-and-authentication.md at 8cec9db, read 2026-11-27).

database-access uses Semantic Scholar Graph API (https://api.semanticscholar.org/graph/v1), a service by Allen Institute for AI; terms: custom API license agreement; terms: https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api/license (as BioMCP 0.9.3's source inventory records it, reviewed 2026-09-27).

database-access uses arXiv API (https://export.arxiv.org/api/query), a service by arXiv (Cornell University); terms: Descriptive metadata is free to use under CC0 1.0; e-prints keep their authors' or publishers' copyright, and redistributing one needs the holder's permission unless its own licence allows it; the legacy API asks for at most one request every three seconds over one connection (arXiv API terms of use, https://info.arxiv.org/help/api/tou.html, read 2026-11-27).

database-access uses bioRxiv and medRxiv API (https://api.biorxiv.org), a service by Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory; terms: The API page states no terms of service; every record it returns carries its preprint's own licence, which governs reuse of that preprint (https://api.biorxiv.org/, read 2026-11-27).

database-access uses Unpaywall API (https://api.unpaywall.org/v2), a service by OurResearch; terms: Not read: unpaywall.org's pages render only in a browser, and the API root (https://api.unpaywall.org/v2) names only its documentation page, whose terms were not read (checked 2026-11-27).
